   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:4bdf8441-c99c-40a3-8b8e-c58dbc2c584f",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bad0d7258385e7c50bbb31a12cb1ec37?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGR-3.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bad0d7258385e7c50bbb31a12cb1ec37?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGR-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bad0d7258385e7c50bbb31a12cb1ec37?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGR-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bad0d7258385e7c50bbb31a12cb1ec37?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGR-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Glen Robson",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A4bdf8441-c99c-40a3-8b8e-c58dbc2c584f",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I think I have discovered the problem in the fedora 33 source:",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "./fcrepo-server/src/main/java/fedora/server/journal/readerwriter/multicast/rmi/RmiTransport.java",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Source code was:",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "194     @Override",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "195     public void closeFile() throws JournalException {",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "196         try {",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "197             super.testStateChange(State.FILE_CLOSED);",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "198             parent.writeDocumentTrailer(xmlWriter);",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "199             xmlWriter.close();",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "201             super.setState(State.FILE_CLOSED);",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "202         } catch (XMLStreamException e) {",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "203             throw new JournalException(e);",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "204         }",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "205     }",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Which meant the RMI process was never calling the remove close function. I changed it to:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "194     @Override",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "195     public void closeFile() throws JournalException {",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "196         try {",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "197             super.testStateChange(State.FILE_CLOSED);",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "198             parent.writeDocumentTrailer(xmlWriter);",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "199             xmlWriter.close();",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "200             writer.close();",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "201             super.setState(State.FILE_CLOSED);",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "202         } catch (XMLStreamException e) {",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "203             throw new JournalException(e);",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "204         } catch (IOException tExcpt) {",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "205             throw new JournalException(tExcpt);",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "206         }",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "207     }",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "i.e. added the writer.close() and it now closes it correctly. I built the source code by downloading the src and running mvn package in the root source dir. I've deployed this rebuilt jar to our Fedora journalling infrastructure and its been working well for the past 2 months. ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
